# The :41840 witness with the ADDRESS of the control-body place taken under the shifted layout (the author,
# CODEX-AUTHOR-OF-EDGE-GENERAL-20261019T064748Z: one projection for every path, no second mapping of a physical address).
# Later's if body is a place of Later's code graph, reached through the result's execution map (native
# lmx_implements_exec_index / self + lmx_implements_code_index, walker OF_EDGE); its cell is written through the place
# (if	: 20), its ADDRESS taken (p: @ if	 -- the pointer is a root own: a pointer field inside a merge operand has no
# D-105 pair), written through the pointer (\p: \p + 7 -> 27), read back by the place path and through the pointer,
# and x reads it: 3 + 27 = 30.  The neighbours keep their distinct values (Later's pad 2, Model's y 4) before and after
# the writes: a wrong slot, a wrong map or a second mapping of the obtained address is a wrong number (81, 82, 83),
# never a coincidence.  Rows: native, the walked root, walked methods, both (Entry 30).
Model:
    int: x 1
    x: x + 1
    int: y 4
    x: x + 1
end: Model

@: p int

Later:
    int: pad 2
    int: x 3
    if: x = 3
        int: t 10
    if\t: 20
    p: @ if\t
    \p: \p + 7
    if: if\t != 27 || \p != 27 || pad != 2
        x: 83
    if: x = 3
        x: x + \p
end: Later

R: merge: Model Later
if: R\x != 3 || R\y != 4 || R\pad != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
call: R
if: R\y != 4 || R\pad != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 82; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: R\x; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
